Producer thread on the four stock trials
- For the 73 calls published after an empty drain, 50 were published by a thread different from the preceding native drain's thread, and 23 by that same thread. Of the four published after an expired budget cutoff, three were on a different thread. The observed timings do not establish a safe main-thread barrier at which to process these later messages.

Interrupted A/B pilot
- Raw capture: build/gameplay-trace/cell-42-getworldspace-drain-ab. Three windows completed before the fourth. The crash report at 13:48:20 records a read at 0x258 (RAX=0) with the faulting instruction in Precision.dll+0119A1F, in a physics stack. The faulting location does not establish the underlying cause. PresentMon exit code 0. No conditions pooled with the four-window retry.
- Pilot DLL SHA256 8D5D430C74F5D82CF277E4C2BD9D6282096DC6336A078E7D961AE6F8273E74C2. The retry adds a second observed-frame check when granting the extra budget, and stops after the four ABBA windows.
